# tally 2.1.7 S5 (G6, NB9): L §5.14.2 Cycles: written orders compose, so `save before spend` and `spend before top`
# order save before top, and a written order, stated or composed, stands for its pair in place of their read edges
# (Kahn 1962). save and top each read konto, which the other changes, on one day (an input day, so the cycle is
# the walk's): save keeps 50.00 PLN (moves 50.00 PLN of 100.00), then top fills konto to 80.00 PLN (30.00 PLN).
# Was (2.1.6): RUN-ORDER decisions save and top read each other.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input day: date
input keep: money PLN
input floor: money PLN
input fee: money PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place kasa: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move save: transfers
  on day
  reads konto
  before spend
  leg cash from konto to savings amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto) - keep)

move spend: transfers
  on day
  reads kasa
  before top
  leg cash from kasa to world amount min(bal(kasa), fee)

move top: transfers
  on day
  reads konto
  leg cash from world to konto amount max(0 PLN, floor - bal(konto))

ask a: flows(save, 2026-01-15)
ask b: flows(top, 2026-01-15)
ask c: bal(konto, 2026-01-15)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  day = 2026-01-15 "s"
  keep = 50.00 PLN "s"
  floor = 80.00 PLN "s"
  fee = 5.00 PLN "s"
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[savings] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[kasa] = 10.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
=== expect
a: 50.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: save
  cut 2026-10-18
b: 30.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: save
  unfulfilled: top
  cut 2026-10-18
c: 80.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: save
  unfulfilled: top
  cut 2026-10-18
